Counts describe posts in this supplied share of the random 20,000-post sample, not how common these experiences are among parents. All 81 yes and 17 near posts were read; none remain unread or were excluded. Each post has one form within its supplied section.

Each post was also tagged yes or no for all four tags. “Tried” includes parenting activities, conversations and arrangements already made; “others” covers people other than the focal child; “bought” requires an explicit purchase or payment statement. “Feeling” includes emotions, emotional appraisals and reactions stated in words, including tears or laughter, but not an emoji or “lol” alone. Unknown ages and speaker characteristics remain unknown.

