### The parent marvels at what their child can remember, understand or create.

6 of 81 posts.

Parents of two- and three-year-olds describe a remembered weekday, whole books recited, independent alphabet writing, stick-figure drawing and translation between family languages. Some ask whether the ability is common because they lack a comparison; others simply share their surprise and pride. One child learns brown immediately while other colours remain less reliable.

- "His mothe said something in Bulgarian, he then looked at me and said the same thing in West Frisian and we were both quite shocked." [ar011-0104]
- "Our 2y4mo can recite the Gruffalo from memory with complete accuracy." [ar018-0049]
- "This morning was the first time he wrote his ABC’s without tracing. I’m super proud of him." [ar061-0022]
