6 of 81 posts.

Children aged two to three answer a correction with a contradiction, move their noise-making to real drums, or turn a request for manners into an effective snack routine. Other posts describe a polite demand not to breathe on the child, kissing the bathroom floor after a hygiene warning, and calling a slap a high five. Parents recount being amused, impressed or humbled even when the original problem remains.

- "She got herself up, walked straight over to her toy drum set and said something to me. […] the pride I felt was suddenly turning to horror as she began to bang away happily at the drums for the next 15 minutes." [ar070-0082]
