### The parent is moved when their child notices distress and tries to comfort someone.

4 of 81 posts.

Two- and three-year-olds offer a grieving parent a cat toy, repeat words of reassurance, worry about a hungry child in a book, or cry when a newborn sister cries. The parents report being surprised by the child’s concern and proud of their empathy. One father describes this in a two-and-a-half-year-old with cerebral palsy whose speech and independent movement are limited.

- "She brought me her cat stuffie and told me to hug it and insisted I close my eyes in a way only a two year old can (aggressively lol). Then she laid her little head on me and said "it's ok Mommy."" [ar038-0034]
