### The parent is proud when their child handles other people with kindness or speaks up for themselves.

3 of 81 posts.

At two to three years, one child keeps trying to make a friend despite rejection, another confronts playground name-calling with parental coaching, and another says rough play hurt. The parents want kindness, resilience or the ability to insist that bodily boundaries be heard. One mother also describes standing up to family as a change from her own childhood fear.

- "I was so impressed and proud of my son and how resilient he was. He kept choosing kindness and it paid off for him. He's only two, but I for some reason I felt very reassured that he's going to do well in life." [ar077-0086]
